${user}` and invokes `claude` with `--max-turns 1` and `--tools ""` (subscription.ts:111) as the sole defenses against agentic behaviour under the user's real credentials. The entire safety claim ("acts as a pure completion engine, no file edits/bash") rests on `--tools ""` being a valid, effective way to disable tools; an empty-string value to a possibly-unrecognized flag is a brittle foundation. Even with turns bounded, injected instructions in the analyzed code can suppress real findings or shape a patch diff, and audit.ts:200-203 will write non-rejected patches straight to the working tree on `--apply`. The grounding gate protects citation integrity, not omissions or patch contents.

